{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jacob-J-Thomas/GraphGoblin/pulls/485","id":5324696891,"node_id":"PR_kwDOU6rh8s8AAAABPWBtOw","html_url":"https://github.com/Jacob-J-Thomas/GraphGoblin/pull/485","diff_url":"https://github.com/Jacob-J-Thomas/GraphGoblin/pull/485.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/Jacob-J-Thomas/GraphGoblin/pull/485.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jacob-J-Thomas/GraphGoblin/issues/485","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jacob-J-Thomas/GraphGoblin/pulls/485/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jacob-J-Thomas/GraphGoblin/pulls/485/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jacob-J-Thomas/GraphGoblin/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jacob-J-Thomas/GraphGoblin/issues/485/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jacob-J-Thomas/GraphGoblin/statuses/5082bc176e92cf3518abb630a5afc0a59c444815","number":485,"state":"open","locked":false,"title":"Classify authored failures and keep engine diagnostics private","user":{"login":"Jacob-J-Thomas","id":92639671,"node_id":"U_kgDOBYWRtw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/92639671?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jacob-J-Thomas","html_url":"https://github.com/Jacob-J-Thomas","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jacob-J-Thomas/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jacob-J-Thomas/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jacob-J-Thomas/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jacob-J-Thomas/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jacob-J-Thomas/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jacob-J-Thomas/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jacob-J-Thomas/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jacob-J-Thomas/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jacob-J-Thomas/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"An authored mutation error currently appears as a resumable internal fault. This change publishes nonresumable `MUTATION_ERROR` failures with the node, operation index/kind and a bounded author diagnostic. Authored Exit evaluation errors use `EXPRESSION_ERROR`. Unexpected failures keep their recovery behavior while newly published run records and events exclude private exception messages, paths and stacks; correlated server logs retain the diagnostic.\n\nThe handling preserves atomic mutations, repair and raw-fallback outcomes, cancellation/deadline precedence, script classification, inference recording order, and subloop recovery metadata. Historical rows and events are unchanged. ADR-0080, the numbered documentation, CHANGELOG and generated API types describe the new-record boundary.\n\nCloses #381. Incorporates the criteria consolidated from #414.\n\nValidation:\n\n- Focused candidate checks: 1,070 tests; final isolated domain coverage: 460 tests, 98.74% lines / 95.98% branches; final engine coverage: 1,812 tests, 96.94% lines / 91.22% branches. Types, lint, schema generation, templates, licences, documentation and contrast checks are recorded in the [implementation evidence](https://github.com/Jacob-J-Thomas/GraphGoblin/blob/5082bc176e92cf3518abb630a5afc0a59c444815/docs/qa/2026-11-15-runtime-failure-implementation/README.md).\n- Independent candidate QA: 18 functional and 13 internal cases on the frozen source/build, with explicit zero-exit receipts and owned-resource cleanup. This includes compiled REST/stdio MCP, real SQLite, the served Edge inspector, controlled fault ports and two native Node script controls. [Candidate evidence](https://github.com/Jacob-J-Thomas/GraphGoblin/blob/5082bc176e92cf3518abb630a5afc0a59c444815/docs/qa/2026-11-15-runtime-failure-candidate/README.md)\n- The original full local `pnpm check` failed during coverage. The packet preserves its complete outputs, later isolated results and unresolved causes in unrelated Windows suites; it does not claim a green full local run. Current publication-head CI remains a separate required gate.\n- The [unchanged-main baseline](https://github.com/Jacob-J-Thomas/GraphGoblin/blob/5082bc176e92cf3518abb630a5afc0a59c444815/docs/qa/2026-11-15-runtime-failure-baseline/README.md) preserves the reproduced behavior and original fixture/supervisor failures, including the missing internal baseline harness exit value.\n\nGPT-6.1 Sol xhigh implemented this slice. Separate Sol xhigh agents performed behavior QA. Claude Opus 5.5 xhigh adversarial review and fresh GPT-6 Astra max exact-head/target sign-off follow green current-head CI, under the shared three-scan cap. This draft is not a merge or owner-acceptance claim.\n\nThe evidence-only publication also records the already merged PR #484's [CI](https://github.com/Jacob-J-Thomas/GraphGoblin/blob/5082bc176e92cf3518abb630a5afc0a59c444815/docs/qa/2026-11-15-poll-dedupe-current-ci/README.md) and [completion](https://github.com/Jacob-J-Thomas/GraphGoblin/blob/5082bc176e92cf3518abb630a5afc0a59c444815/docs/qa/2026-11-15-poll-dedupe-completion/README.md). The delivery register keeps subsequent #410, #419 and launcher work separate.\n","labels":[],"milestone":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"created_at":"2026-11-15T16:23:24Z","updated_at":"2026-11-15T16:23:45Z","closed_at":null,"merged_at":null,"merge_commit_sha":"5db4567e252e503d44db79e1216f52312616b31f","assignee":null,"assignees":[],"requested_reviewers":[],"requested_teams":[],"head":{"label":"Jacob-J-Thomas:codex/gg-20261115-mutation-failures","ref":"codex/gg-20261115-mutation-failures","repo":{"id":1403707890,"node_id":"R_kgDOU6rh8g","name":"GraphGoblin","full_name":"Jacob-J-Thomas/GraphGoblin","owner":{"login":"Jacob-J-Thomas","id":92639671,"node_id":"U_kgDOBYWRtw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/92639671?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jacob-J-Thomas","html_url":"htt